# .dockerignore — what `docker build` may see of the repo, the build context of backend/Dockerfile (OPS-1).
#
# An allowlist: everything is shut out, then only what the image needs is let back in. So a new file at
# the root stays out by default — a .env with secrets, a sheet in private/ with real shop data (ops rule,
# CLAUDE.md rule 10). An image gets pushed to a registry (OPS-2): whatever goes in can be pulled out again.

# Shut out everything...
*
# ...then let in the two folders the Dockerfile copies from.
!backend
!frontend

# Inside them, shut out again what is secret, and what the build makes for itself.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
backend/.venv
backend/staticfiles
backend/.pytest_cache
backend/.mypy_cache
backend/.ruff_cache
backend/.import_linter_cache
backend/.coverage
backend/htmlcov
frontend/node_modules
frontend/.next
frontend/out
frontend/coverage
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/next-env.d.ts
